WEBVTT

00:00:07.124 --> 00:00:08.952
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.210
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:12.051 --> 00:00:12.687
Mary!

00:00:12.859 --> 00:00:13.481
No!

00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:16.452
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.075
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:21.145 --> 00:00:22.557
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:23.249 --> 00:00:24.383
I can't do this alone.

00:00:26.847 --> 00:00:27.788
No!

00:00:30.403 --> 00:00:31.510
We got work to do.

00:00:32.229 --> 00:00:34.613
This was dad's single
most valuable possession.

00:00:34.681 --> 00:00:36.825
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:36.963 --> 00:00:38.910
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:38.993 --> 00:00:40.266
You know, saving people,

00:00:40.349 --> 00:00:41.373
Hunting things,

00:00:41.428 --> 00:00:42.342
Family business.

00:00:42.425 --> 00:00:42.840
No.

00:00:42.951 --> 00:00:44.267
I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:44.361 --> 00:00:45.785
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:45.844 --> 00:00:47.228
Sam, You know we're gonna find dad,

00:00:47.256 --> 00:00:47.662
Right?

00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:50.668
Yeah. I know.

00:01:32.455 --> 00:01:33.248
Nervous flyer?

00:01:34.104 --> 00:01:35.397
It's that obvious, huh?

00:01:36.507 --> 00:01:38.775
You know, what are the odds
of dying in a plane crash?

00:01:38.981 --> 00:01:39.749
I mean, what

00:01:39.918 --> 00:01:40.949
20,000 to one?

00:01:44.809 --> 00:01:45.334
Wow.

00:01:46.084 --> 00:01:47.996
That's, uh, really
reassuring. Thank you.

00:02:13.872 --> 00:02:14.359
Thanks.

00:02:15.146 --> 00:02:15.615
Miranda,

00:02:15.784 --> 00:02:16.421
How are you today?

00:02:16.605 --> 00:02:17.842
I'm doing just fine, Chuck.

00:02:19.454 --> 00:02:20.616
Welcome aboard.

00:02:21.328 --> 00:02:24.083
15c towards the back of
the plane, on the right.

00:02:27.041 --> 00:02:28.259
Have a nice flight, sir.

00:02:31.102 --> 00:02:32.470
Oh, I'm counting on it.

00:02:37.786 --> 00:02:38.442
Um...

00:02:40.241 --> 00:02:41.647
Uh, 11F,

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.615
That's the middle of the
plane, on... Thank you

00:02:45.823 --> 00:02:46.535
...the left.

00:02:58.529 --> 00:02:59.241
Excuse me.

00:03:00.044 --> 00:03:01.319
Do you know how long we've been up?

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:03.793
Oh, uh... about 40 minutes.

00:03:04.823 --> 00:03:05.386
Wow.

00:03:05.682 --> 00:03:07.050
Time really does fly, huh?

00:03:10.403 --> 00:03:11.115
Excuse me.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.670
I've got to stretch my legs.

00:03:39.332 --> 00:03:40.661
You, what the hell are you doing?!

00:04:52.793 --> 00:04:53.674
Morning, sunshine.

00:04:55.039 --> 00:04:55.807
What time is it?

00:04:55.957 --> 00:04:57.269
Huh, It's about 5:45.

00:04:57.419 --> 00:04:58.131
In the morning?

00:04:58.206 --> 00:04:58.600
Yep.

00:04:58.806 --> 00:04:59.871
Where does the day go?

00:05:01.933 --> 00:05:03.020
Did you get any sleep last night?

00:05:03.226 --> 00:05:04.575
Yeah, I grabbed a couple hours.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:05.288
You, liar

00:05:06.256 --> 00:05:07.381
'Cause I was up at 3:00,

00:05:08.131 --> 00:05:09.930
And you were watching a
George Foreman infomercial.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:10.808
Hey, what can I say?

00:05:10.864 --> 00:05:11.745
It's riveting tv.

00:05:12.176 --> 00:05:13.563
When was the last time you
got a good night's sleep?

00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:14.388
I don't know,

00:05:14.463 --> 00:05:16.053
A little while, I guess.
It's not a big deal

00:05:16.241 --> 00:05:16.971
Yeah, it is.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.864
I appreciate your concern.

00:05:18.902 --> 00:05:20.232
I'm not concerned about you.

00:05:20.251 --> 00:05:22.781
It's your job to keep my ass
alive, so I need you sharp.

00:05:24.198 --> 00:05:25.773
Seriously, are you still
having nightmares about Jess?

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:31.807
Yeah.

00:05:33.585 --> 00:05:35.272
But it's not just her. It's everything.

00:05:35.703 --> 00:05:37.408
I just forgot, you know? This job.

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:39.805
Man, it gets to you.

00:05:40.123 --> 00:05:42.129
You can't let it. You can't
bring it home like that.

00:05:43.441 --> 00:05:44.003
So, what?

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:44.603
All this it...

00:05:44.915 --> 00:05:45.946
Never keeps you up at night?

00:05:47.108 --> 00:05:47.576
Never?

00:05:47.932 --> 00:05:48.645
You're never afraid?

00:05:48.926 --> 00:05:49.807
No, not really.

00:05:58.129 --> 00:05:58.913
That's not fear.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:01.125
That is precaution.

00:06:01.706 --> 00:06:02.605
All right, whatever.

00:06:02.643 --> 00:06:03.749
I'm too tired to argue.

00:06:12.703 --> 00:06:13.246
Hello?

00:06:13.525 --> 00:06:13.974
Dean,

00:06:14.237 --> 00:06:15.905
It's Jerry Panowski.

00:06:16.886 --> 00:06:18.901
You and your dad helped
me out a couple years back.

00:06:19.985 --> 00:06:20.937
Oh, all right,

00:06:20.981 --> 00:06:23.771
Yeah, up in kittanning,
Pennsylvania, the poltergeist thing.

00:06:24.213 --> 00:06:25.143
It's not back, is it?

00:06:25.342 --> 00:06:25.807
No.

00:06:26.184 --> 00:06:26.715
No.

00:06:27.955 --> 00:06:28.774
Thank god, no.

00:06:30.254 --> 00:06:32.003
But it's something else, and...

00:06:32.512 --> 00:06:33.862
Well, I think it could be a lot worse.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.058
What is it?

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:36.648
Can we talk in person?

00:06:42.427 --> 00:06:44.176
Thanks for making the trip so quick.

00:06:44.281 --> 00:06:46.823
I ought to be doing you guys a
favor, not the other way around.

00:06:47.775 --> 00:06:49.280
Dean and your dad really helped me out.

00:06:49.878 --> 00:06:51.516
Yeah, he told me. It was a poltergeist?

00:06:51.583 --> 00:06:52.225
Poltergeist?

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.328
Man, I loved that movie.

00:06:53.372 --> 00:06:55.232
Hey, nobody's talking
to you. Keep walking.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.907
Damn right it was a poltergeist
practically tore our house apart.

00:06:59.903 --> 00:07:00.855
Tell you something

00:07:01.493 --> 00:07:02.799
If it wasn't for you and your dad,

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:04.061
I probably wouldn't be alive.

00:07:06.261 --> 00:07:08.033
Your dad said you were off
at college. Is that right?

00:07:08.652 --> 00:07:09.870
Yeah, I was. I'm...

00:07:10.158 --> 00:07:11.287
Taking some time off.

00:07:11.575 --> 00:07:13.169
Well, he was real proud
of you. I could tell.

00:07:13.612 --> 00:07:14.962
He talked about you all the time.

00:07:16.331 --> 00:07:16.951
He did?

00:07:17.327 --> 00:07:18.323
Yeah, you bet he did.

00:07:18.833 --> 00:07:20.781
Oh, hey, I tried to get
ahold of him, but I couldn't.

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:22.309
How's he doing, anyway?

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:24.434
He's, um

00:07:25.023 --> 00:07:26.352
Wrapped up in a job right now.

00:07:26.617 --> 00:07:28.145
Well, we're missing the old man.

00:07:28.411 --> 00:07:29.363
We get sam.

00:07:29.518 --> 00:07:30.691
Even trade, huh?

00:07:31.223 --> 00:07:32.684
No, not by a long shot.

00:07:33.304 --> 00:07:34.964
I got something I want you guys to hear.

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:37.930
I listened to this.

00:07:38.439 --> 00:07:38.926
Well,

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:40.653
It sounded like it was up your alley

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:42.889
Normally I wouldn't have access to this.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.737
It's the cockpit voice recorder
for united britannia flight 2485.

00:07:47.025 --> 00:07:47.933
It was one of ours.

00:07:48.456 --> 00:07:48.905
Mayday

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.221
Took off from here,

00:08:12.783 --> 00:08:14.555
Crashed about 200 miles south.

00:08:14.834 --> 00:08:16.945
Now, they're saying mechanical failure.

00:08:17.147 --> 00:08:19.490
Cabin depressurized
somehow. Nobody knows why.

00:08:19.848 --> 00:08:21.145
Over 100 people on board.

00:08:21.931 --> 00:08:23.083
Only seven got out alive.

00:08:24.056 --> 00:08:24.837
Pilot was one.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.380
His name is chuck lambert.
He's a good friend of mine.

00:08:27.962 --> 00:08:28.929
Chuck is, uh...

00:08:30.589 --> 00:08:31.887
Well, he's pretty broken up about it,

00:08:32.708 --> 00:08:33.581
Like it was his fault.

00:08:34.416 --> 00:08:35.223
You don't think it was?

00:08:35.766 --> 00:08:36.614
No, I don't.

00:08:37.334 --> 00:08:37.810
Jerry,

00:08:37.996 --> 00:08:39.836
We're gonna need passenger manifests,

00:08:39.921 --> 00:08:41.390
Hum...a list of survivors.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:41.907
All right.

00:08:42.026 --> 00:08:42.661
And huh...

00:08:42.741 --> 00:08:44.277
Any way we can take a
look at the wreckage?

00:08:44.958 --> 00:08:46.190
The other stuff is no problem,

00:08:46.243 --> 00:08:47.064
But the wreckage

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:50.803
Fellas, the ntsb has it locked
down in an evidence warehouse.

00:08:51.782 --> 00:08:53.292
No way I've got that kind of clearance.

00:08:55.858 --> 00:08:56.348
No problem.

00:09:01.786 --> 00:09:02.237
Hey

00:09:02.395 --> 00:09:02.859
Hi.

00:09:05.825 --> 00:09:06.831
You've been in there forever.

00:09:08.358 --> 00:09:09.391
You can't rush perfection.

00:09:10.132 --> 00:09:11.245
Homeland security?

00:09:12.423 --> 00:09:13.337
That's pretty illegal,

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.118
Even for us.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:15.456
Yeah, well,

00:09:15.495 --> 00:09:16.820
It's something new, you know?

00:09:16.833 --> 00:09:18.528
People haven't seen it a thousand times.

00:09:23.337 --> 00:09:24.260
All right, so, what do you got?

00:09:24.479 --> 00:09:25.121
Well,

00:09:25.136 --> 00:09:27.702
There's definitely E.V.P. On
the cockpit voice recorder.

00:09:27.812 --> 00:09:28.156
Yeah?

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:28.735
Listen.

00:09:36.412 --> 00:09:37.429
"No survivors"?

00:09:38.321 --> 00:09:39.051
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:39.061 --> 00:09:40.532
There were seven survivors.

00:09:41.122 --> 00:09:41.748
Got me.

00:09:43.996 --> 00:09:45.514
So, what are you
thinking? A haunted flight?

00:09:45.959 --> 00:09:47.587
There's a long history of spirits and

00:09:47.634 --> 00:09:49.638
Death omens on planes and ships,

00:09:49.685 --> 00:09:50.749
Like phantom travelers.

00:09:50.796 --> 00:09:51.203
Mm-Hmm

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.160
Or remember flight 401?

00:09:53.394 --> 00:09:53.848
Right

00:09:54.068 --> 00:09:54.835
The one that crashed,

00:09:54.882 --> 00:09:56.384
The airline salvaged
some of this parts,*

00:09:56.447 --> 00:09:57.527
Put it in other planes,

00:09:57.836 --> 00:10:00.074
Then the spirit of the pilot and
copilot haunted those flights.

00:10:00.137 --> 00:10:00.481
Right.

00:10:00.544 --> 00:10:01.029
Yep.

00:10:01.984 --> 00:10:03.205
Maybe we got a similar deal.

00:10:03.941 --> 00:10:06.320
All rigth so, survivors which
one do you want to talk to first?

00:10:06.373 --> 00:10:08.094
Third on the list Max Jaffey.

00:10:08.188 --> 00:10:08.767
Why him?

00:10:08.814 --> 00:10:10.020
For one, he's from around here.

00:10:10.072 --> 00:10:10.823
And two,

00:10:11.402 --> 00:10:12.780
If anyone saw anything weird.

00:10:13.421 --> 00:10:13.954
He did.

00:10:15.112 --> 00:10:15.973
What makes you say that?

00:10:16.317 --> 00:10:17.554
Well, I spoke to his mother,

00:10:18.359 --> 00:10:19.706
And she told me where to find him.

00:10:22.447 --> 00:10:23.370
I don't understand.

00:10:23.382 --> 00:10:25.329
I already spoke with homeland security.

00:10:25.681 --> 00:10:26.270
Right.

00:10:26.776 --> 00:10:28.308
Some new information has come up.

00:10:28.544 --> 00:10:30.464
So if you could just
answer a couple questions...

00:10:30.669 --> 00:10:32.016
Just before the plane went down,

00:10:32.707 --> 00:10:35.031
Did you notice anything unusual?

00:10:35.368 --> 00:10:36.092
Like what?

00:10:36.884 --> 00:10:38.113
Strange lights,

00:10:38.787 --> 00:10:40.101
Weird noises, maybe...

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.208
Voices.

00:10:43.128 --> 00:10:43.936
No, nothing.

00:10:45.869 --> 00:10:46.711
Mr. Joffey

00:10:47.671 --> 00:10:48.143
Jaffey.

00:10:48.446 --> 00:10:48.951
Jaffey.

00:10:49.086 --> 00:10:50.231
You checked yourself in here,

00:10:50.349 --> 00:10:50.804
Right?

00:10:52.019 --> 00:10:52.815
Can I ask why?

00:10:53.312 --> 00:10:54.619
I was a little stressed.

00:10:54.639 --> 00:10:56.490
I survived a plane crash.

00:10:58.156 --> 00:10:58.733
And that's

00:10:58.833 --> 00:10:59.629
What terrified you?

00:10:59.669 --> 00:11:00.803
That's what you were afraid of?

00:11:00.902 --> 00:11:03.410
I... I don't want to
talk about this anymore.

00:11:03.589 --> 00:11:05.380
I think maybe you did
see something up there.

00:11:06.415 --> 00:11:07.410
We need to know what.

00:11:08.478 --> 00:11:08.956
No.

00:11:09.095 --> 00:11:10.170
No, I was...

00:11:10.309 --> 00:11:11.065
Delusional

00:11:11.844 --> 00:11:12.800
Seeing things.

00:11:14.105 --> 00:11:15.125
He was seeing things.

00:11:18.676 --> 00:11:19.271
It's okay.

00:11:20.737 --> 00:11:23.664
Then just tell us what you
thought you saw, please.

00:11:28.307 --> 00:11:29.038
There was...

00:11:29.277 --> 00:11:29.849
This...

00:11:30.198 --> 00:11:30.866
Man.

00:11:32.551 --> 00:11:33.441
And, uh,

00:11:33.536 --> 00:11:34.951
He had these...

00:11:36.047 --> 00:11:36.670
Eyes...

00:11:36.765 --> 00:11:37.512
These, uh...

00:11:39.587 --> 00:11:40.795
Black eyes.

00:11:42.607 --> 00:11:44.435
And I saw him

00:11:45.215 --> 00:11:47.377
I thought I saw him...

00:11:51.319 --> 00:11:51.923
What?

00:11:54.214 --> 00:11:56.391
He opened the emergency exit.

00:11:58.586 --> 00:11:59.190
But that's...

00:11:59.238 --> 00:12:00.351
That's impossible,

00:12:00.764 --> 00:12:02.022
Right? I mean, I looked it up.

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:02.944
There's something like

00:12:03.103 --> 00:12:05.200
Two tons of pressure on that door.

00:12:07.364 --> 00:12:07.936
Yeah...

00:12:08.842 --> 00:12:09.732
This man, huh...

00:12:09.812 --> 00:12:12.307
Did he seem to appear and disappear.

00:12:12.564 --> 00:12:14.948
Rapidly.It would look
something like a mirage.

00:12:16.733 --> 00:12:18.052
What are you, nuts?

00:12:20.293 --> 00:12:21.437
He was a passenger.

00:12:21.469 --> 00:12:23.376
He was sitting right in front of me.

00:12:30.485 --> 00:12:31.645
Say here we are

00:12:31.757 --> 00:12:33.902
George Phelps, seat 20c.

00:12:34.538 --> 00:12:35.047
Hmm.

00:12:36.002 --> 00:12:38.196
Man, I don't care how strong you are.

00:12:40.691 --> 00:12:42.725
Even yoked up on pcp or something,

00:12:43.109 --> 00:12:46.097
No way you can open up an
emergency door during a flight.

00:12:47.069 --> 00:12:48.086
Not if you're human.

00:12:49.437 --> 00:12:51.423
But maybe this guy
George was something else

00:12:51.754 --> 00:12:53.915
Some kind of creature,
maybe, in human form.

00:12:54.344 --> 00:12:56.124
Does that look like a
creature's lair to you?

00:13:04.756 --> 00:13:06.059
This is your late husband?

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.523
Yes, that was my george.

00:13:09.344 --> 00:13:10.441
And you said he was a...

00:13:11.299 --> 00:13:12.094
Dentist?

00:13:12.514 --> 00:13:13.097
Mm-Hmm.

00:13:14.374 --> 00:13:16.683
He was headed to a convention in Denver.

00:13:19.547 --> 00:13:21.594
Do you know that he
was petrified to fly?

00:13:25.257 --> 00:13:26.666
For him to go like that...

00:13:29.313 --> 00:13:30.553
How long were you married?

00:13:32.957 --> 00:13:34.159
13 years.

00:13:34.916 --> 00:13:36.118
In all that time,

00:13:37.714 --> 00:13:39.442
Did you ever notice anything...

00:13:39.836 --> 00:13:41.339
Strange about him,

00:13:41.864 --> 00:13:43.479
Anything out of the ordinary?

00:13:46.684 --> 00:13:47.379
Well...

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.682
Uh, he had acid reflux,

00:13:51.813 --> 00:13:52.883
If that's what you mean.

00:13:57.017 --> 00:13:58.202
I mean it goes without saying.

00:13:58.221 --> 00:13:59.635
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:14:00.037 --> 00:14:01.652
A middle-Aged dentist with an ulcer

00:14:01.671 --> 00:14:03.399
Is not exactly evil personified.

00:14:04.169 --> 00:14:06.310
You know what we need to do is
get inside that ntsb warehouse,

00:14:06.328 --> 00:14:07.812
Check out the wreckage.

00:14:09.654 --> 00:14:10.555
Okay.

00:14:10.799 --> 00:14:11.764
But if we're gonna go that route,

00:14:11.793 --> 00:14:12.638
We'd better look the part.

00:14:19.016 --> 00:14:21.253
I look like one of the blues brothers.

00:14:21.572 --> 00:14:22.398
No, you don't.

00:14:22.886 --> 00:14:24.107
You look more like a...

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:25.854
Seventh-Grader at his first dance.

00:14:28.694 --> 00:14:29.896
I hate this thing.

00:14:29.933 --> 00:14:30.365
Hey.

00:14:30.741 --> 00:14:32.450
You want into that warehouse or not?

00:15:16.444 --> 00:15:17.158
What is that?

00:15:18.322 --> 00:15:19.487
It's an E.M.F. Meter...

00:15:19.937 --> 00:15:21.646
Reads electromagnetic frequencies.

00:15:22.437 --> 00:15:24.291
Yeah, I know what an E.M.F. Meter is,

00:15:24.309 --> 00:15:26.751
But why does that one look
like a busted-Up walkman?

00:15:27.804 --> 00:15:29.006
That's what I made it out of.

00:15:29.757 --> 00:15:30.714
It's homemade.

00:15:32.818 --> 00:15:34.677
Yeah, I can see that.

00:16:01.219 --> 00:16:02.778
Check out emergency door handle.

00:16:08.433 --> 00:16:09.372
What is this stuff?

00:16:09.503 --> 00:16:10.818
One way to find out.

00:16:23.681 --> 00:16:24.864
Homeland security?

00:16:25.697 --> 00:16:26.166
What?

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:27.706
One team of you guys isn't enough?

00:16:28.345 --> 00:16:29.190
What are you talking about?

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.539
Two of your buddies went
inside not five minutes ago.

00:17:11.927 --> 00:17:13.918
These monkey suits do come in handy.

00:17:15.439 --> 00:17:16.209
Listen Chuck

00:17:16.378 --> 00:17:17.429
It's like getting back on a horse,

00:17:17.977 --> 00:17:19.460
Only in this case, a little twin engine.

00:17:19.779 --> 00:17:20.606
Not even a horse

00:17:20.756 --> 00:17:21.545
More like a pony.

00:17:22.561 --> 00:17:23.481
I'll be right there with you too.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.490
Anytime you feel like you don't
want the wheel, I'll take over.

00:17:26.411 --> 00:17:27.218
Look, Chuck,

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:28.927
We don't have to do this today.

00:17:29.303 --> 00:17:30.110
I'm not trying to rush you.

00:17:31.032 --> 00:17:31.746
No, the...

00:17:32.854 --> 00:17:33.849
The waiting is worse.

00:17:36.328 --> 00:17:38.169
Okay, they're filling
up the tank. Then we go.

00:18:11.365 --> 00:18:11.928
Huh.

00:18:13.599 --> 00:18:15.045
This stuff is covered in sulfur.

00:18:15.327 --> 00:18:15.947
You're sure?

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:17.487
Take a look for yourself.

00:18:17.506 --> 00:18:18.876
"You effin' piece of..."

00:18:18.876 --> 00:18:20.210
If you fellows will excuse me,

00:18:20.247 --> 00:18:21.675
I have an idiot to fire.

00:18:28.603 --> 00:18:28.998
Hmm.

00:18:29.974 --> 00:18:32.754
Here is not too many things that
leave behind a sulfuric residue.

00:18:32.857 --> 00:18:33.833
Demonic possession?

00:18:34.378 --> 00:18:37.495
It would explain how a mortal man would have
the strength to open up an emergency hatch.

00:18:37.666 --> 00:18:39.074
If the guy was possessed,

00:18:39.318 --> 00:18:40.013
It's possible.

00:18:40.316 --> 00:18:42.701
This goes way beyond
floating over a bed or

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:43.602
Barfing pea soup.

00:18:43.659 --> 00:18:45.180
What mean it's one thing
to possess a person,

00:18:45.217 --> 00:18:47.152
But to use them to take
down an entire airplane?

00:18:47.283 --> 00:18:48.992
You ever heard of
something like this before?

00:18:49.182 --> 00:18:49.707
Never.

00:18:55.623 --> 00:18:56.299
I'm ready.

00:18:56.506 --> 00:18:57.332
Let's do this.

00:19:05.588 --> 00:19:06.395
How you feeling?

00:19:06.658 --> 00:19:07.466
I feel great.

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:09.531
You'll be back flying
jumbos before you know it.

00:19:09.907 --> 00:19:10.752
I hope so.

00:19:14.472 --> 00:19:15.298
How long we been up?

00:19:15.862 --> 00:19:17.608
Huh... Almost 40 minutes.

00:19:17.965 --> 00:19:18.416
Wow.

00:19:18.773 --> 00:19:19.768
Time really does fly.

00:19:47.049 --> 00:19:47.669
So,

00:19:48.063 --> 00:19:50.166
Every religion in every world culture

00:19:50.223 --> 00:19:53.077
Has the concept of demons
and demonic possession, right?

00:19:53.426 --> 00:19:56.374
I mean christian, native
american, hindu. You name it.

00:19:56.468 --> 00:19:58.140
Yeah, but none of them
describe anything like this.

00:19:58.234 --> 00:19:59.360
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:19:59.398 --> 00:20:00.806
You see according to japanese beliefs,

00:20:00.844 --> 00:20:03.567
Certain demons are
behind certain disasters,

00:20:03.612 --> 00:20:04.476
Both natural

00:20:04.589 --> 00:20:05.453
And man-Made

00:20:05.509 --> 00:20:07.762
One causes earthquakes.
Another causes disease.

00:20:07.781 --> 00:20:09.340
And this one causes plane crashes?

00:20:13.607 --> 00:20:14.771
All right, so, what?

00:20:14.809 --> 00:20:16.837
We have a demonthat's
evolved with the times

00:20:16.875 --> 00:20:18.602
And found a way to
ratchet up the body count?

00:20:19.522 --> 00:20:20.106
Yeah.

00:20:21.252 --> 00:20:21.853
You know,

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:25.120
Who knows how many planes it's
brought down before this one?

00:20:30.026 --> 00:20:30.533
What?

00:20:32.091 --> 00:20:34.082
I don't know, man. This
isn't our normal gig.

00:20:34.645 --> 00:20:36.298
I mean, demons, they
don't want anything just

00:20:36.373 --> 00:20:38.251
Death and destructionfor its own sake.

00:20:39.246 --> 00:20:39.960
This is big.

00:20:41.389 --> 00:20:42.516
I wish dad was here.

00:20:43.587 --> 00:20:44.845
Yeah. Me too.

00:20:51.609 --> 00:20:51.984
Hello?

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.167
Dean it's Jerry

00:20:53.355 --> 00:20:54.069
Oh, hey, Jerry.

00:20:54.369 --> 00:20:55.327
My pilot friend...

00:20:57.318 --> 00:20:58.444
Chuck Lambert, is dead.

00:21:00.437 --> 00:21:00.925
Wha...

00:21:01.301 --> 00:21:02.446
Jerry, I'm sorry. What happened?

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:04.850
He and his buddy went
up in a small twin.

00:21:04.925 --> 00:21:05.939
About an hour ago.

00:21:06.578 --> 00:21:07.423
The plane went down.

00:21:07.799 --> 00:21:08.587
Where'd this happen?

00:21:08.907 --> 00:21:11.066
About 60 miles west
of here, near nazareth.

00:21:11.632 --> 00:21:13.078
I'll try to ignore the irony in that.

00:21:13.322 --> 00:21:13.885
I'm sorry?

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:14.637
Nothing.

00:21:15.369 --> 00:21:17.303
Jerry hang in there, all right?
We'll catch up with you soon.

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:20.258
Another crash?

00:21:20.465 --> 00:21:20.990
Yeah.

00:21:21.366 --> 00:21:21.836
Let's go.

00:21:22.042 --> 00:21:22.587
Where?

00:21:23.282 --> 00:21:23.901
Nazareth.

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:36.792
Sulfur?

00:21:39.498 --> 00:21:40.681
Well, that's great.

00:21:41.414 --> 00:21:44.174
All right, that's two plane
crashes involving Chuck Lambert.

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:46.278
This demon sounds likeit was after him.

00:21:46.684 --> 00:21:47.773
With all due respect to Chuck,

00:21:48.863 --> 00:21:50.966
If that's the case, that
would be the good news.

00:21:51.379 --> 00:21:52.186
What's the bad news?

00:21:52.374 --> 00:21:54.947
Chuck's plane went down
exactly 40 minutes into flight.

00:21:55.112 --> 00:21:55.995
And get this

00:21:56.145 --> 00:21:57.741
So did flight 2485.

00:21:58.042 --> 00:21:58.849
40 minutes?

00:21:59.262 --> 00:21:59.938
What does that mean?

00:22:00.521 --> 00:22:01.835
It's biblical numerology.

00:22:02.098 --> 00:22:04.089
You know Noah's ark,
it rained for 40days.

00:22:04.145 --> 00:22:05.122
The number means death.

00:22:05.518 --> 00:22:06.250
I went back,

00:22:06.325 --> 00:22:08.992
And there have been six plane
crashes over the last decade

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:11.809
That all went down
exactly 40 minutes in.

00:22:12.861 --> 00:22:13.743
Any survivors?

00:22:14.419 --> 00:22:14.889
No.

00:22:15.331 --> 00:22:15.856
Or not

00:22:15.932 --> 00:22:17.002
Until now,at least

00:22:17.021 --> 00:22:19.312
Not until flight 2485, for some reason.

00:22:20.363 --> 00:22:21.809
And the cockpit voice recorder

00:22:21.922 --> 00:22:23.180
Remember what the E.V.P. Said?

00:22:23.481 --> 00:22:24.345
"No survivors."

00:22:28.331 --> 00:22:29.702
It's going after all the survivors.

00:22:30.922 --> 00:22:32.012
Something finish the job.

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:36.427
Really?

00:22:37.046 --> 00:22:38.812
Well, thank you for taking our survey,

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:40.145
And if you do plan to fly,

00:22:40.164 --> 00:22:43.018
Please don't forget your friendsat
united britannia airlines.

00:22:43.751 --> 00:22:44.220
Thanks.

00:22:44.671 --> 00:22:45.309
All right.

00:22:45.424 --> 00:22:48.072
That takes care of Blaines
Anderson and Dennis Holloway.

00:22:48.186 --> 00:22:49.557
They're not flying anytime soon.

00:22:49.614 --> 00:22:52.149
So our only wildcard is the
flight attendant amanda walker.

00:22:52.412 --> 00:22:52.937
Right

00:22:52.975 --> 00:22:55.078
Her sister Karen said her flight
leaves Indianapolis at 8:00.

00:22:55.116 --> 00:22:56.675
Yeah but it's her first
night backon the job.

00:22:56.712 --> 00:22:58.064
That sounds like just our luck.

00:22:58.383 --> 00:22:59.998
Dean, this is a 5-Hour drive made

00:23:00.129 --> 00:23:01.575
Even with you behind the wheel.

00:23:02.159 --> 00:23:03.724
Call amanda's cellphone again,

00:23:03.742 --> 00:23:05.066
See if we can't head
her off at the pass.

00:23:05.121 --> 00:23:06.482
I already left her three voice messages.

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:08.587
She must have turned her cellphone off.

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:11.382
God,we're never gonna make it.

00:23:11.438 --> 00:23:12.127
We'll make it.

00:23:26.462 --> 00:23:27.096
Right there.

00:23:27.208 --> 00:23:28.326
They're boarding in 30 minutes.

00:23:28.475 --> 00:23:29.052
Okay.

00:23:29.593 --> 00:23:30.953
We still have some cards to play.

00:23:31.004 --> 00:23:31.992
We need to find a phone.

00:23:35.175 --> 00:23:36.107
Airport Services.

00:23:36.218 --> 00:23:37.299
Hi. Gate 13.

00:23:37.369 --> 00:23:38.524
<i>Who are you calling, Sir</i>

00:23:38.636 --> 00:23:40.253
I'm trying to contact an Amanda Walker.

00:23:40.275 --> 00:23:42.168
She's a flight attendant
on flight, um...

00:23:42.311 --> 00:23:43.588
Flight 424.

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:44.755
<i>"Amanda walker,"</i>

00:23:45.019 --> 00:23:46.737
<i>"Amanda Walker, you have a phone call"</i>

00:23:46.825 --> 00:23:48.630
<i>"White courtesy phone, gate 13."</i>

00:23:51.569 --> 00:23:52.626
Come on.

00:23:54.233 --> 00:23:55.467
This is amanda walker.

00:23:55.841 --> 00:23:56.611
Miss walker.

00:23:57.052 --> 00:23:58.862
Hi, this is Dr. James Headfield

00:23:58.884 --> 00:24:01.064
From st. Francis memorial hospital.

00:24:01.394 --> 00:24:03.222
We have a Karen Walker here.

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:04.125
Why Karen?

00:24:04.169 --> 00:24:06.282
Nothing serious just
a minor car accident,

00:24:06.317 --> 00:24:07.836
But she was injured, so

00:24:07.968 --> 00:24:10.962
Wa-Wait, that's impossible. I
just got off the phone with her.

00:24:14.227 --> 00:24:14.844
You what?

00:24:14.932 --> 00:24:15.790
Five minutes ago.

00:24:15.834 --> 00:24:18.499
She's at her house,
cramming for a final.

00:24:18.521 --> 00:24:19.467
Who is this?

00:24:20.668 --> 00:24:21.681
Uh, well...

00:24:22.099 --> 00:24:23.200
There must be some mistake.

00:24:23.222 --> 00:24:25.248
And how would you even know I was here?

00:24:26.987 --> 00:24:28.594
Is this one of Vince's friends?

00:24:30.243 --> 00:24:31.322
Guilty as charged.

00:24:32.136 --> 00:24:34.206
Wow. This is unbelievable.

00:24:35.065 --> 00:24:36.694
He's really sorry.

00:24:37.333 --> 00:24:38.918
Well, you tell him to
mind his own business

00:24:38.962 --> 00:24:40.723
And stay out of my life, okay?

00:24:40.811 --> 00:24:41.733
Yes, but...

00:24:42.085 --> 00:24:43.758
He really needs to see you tonight,

00:24:44.089 --> 00:24:44.815
So

00:24:44.925 --> 00:24:46.401
No, I'm sorry. It's too late.

00:24:46.599 --> 00:24:47.634
Don't be like that.

00:24:48.098 --> 00:24:49.199
Come on. The guy's

00:24:49.354 --> 00:24:50.983
A mess. Really. It's pathetic.

00:24:52.326 --> 00:24:53.009
Really?

00:24:53.229 --> 00:24:53.977
Oh, yeah.

00:24:54.638 --> 00:24:56.157
Look, I've got to go. Um...

00:24:56.168 --> 00:24:58.260
Tell him to call me when I land.

00:24:58.414 --> 00:25:00.176
No, no. Wait, Amanda. Amanda!

00:25:06.892 --> 00:25:07.817
How are you?

00:25:09.226 --> 00:25:10.393
Hey, boss. Hey

00:25:18.370 --> 00:25:19.272
Damn it!

00:25:19.779 --> 00:25:20.858
So close.

00:25:23.368 --> 00:25:25.063
All right, it's time for plan "B."

00:25:25.537 --> 00:25:26.594
We're getting on that plane.

00:25:26.704 --> 00:25:28.377
Oh,oh,Now, just hold on a second.

00:25:28.476 --> 00:25:29.092
Dean,

00:25:29.225 --> 00:25:30.392
That plane is leaving

00:25:30.436 --> 00:25:31.955
With over 100 passengers on board,

00:25:31.977 --> 00:25:32.902
And if we're right,

00:25:33.541 --> 00:25:34.840
That plane is gonna crash.

00:25:34.994 --> 00:25:35.632
I know.

00:25:35.743 --> 00:25:36.315
Okay.

00:25:36.408 --> 00:25:39.094
We're getting on the plane, we need
to find that demon and exorcise it.

00:25:39.138 --> 00:25:41.274
I'll get the tickets. You get
whatever you can out of the trunk.

00:25:41.318 --> 00:25:42.507
Whatever that will make
it through the security.

00:25:42.573 --> 00:25:43.872
Meet me back here in five minutes.

00:25:45.876 --> 00:25:46.889
Are you okay?

00:25:49.256 --> 00:25:50.533
No, not really.

00:25:51.810 --> 00:25:52.955
What? What's wrong?

00:25:55.124 --> 00:25:57.150
Well, I kind of have
this problem with, uh...

00:25:59.285 --> 00:26:00.100
Flying?

00:26:00.519 --> 00:26:02.236
It's never really been
an issue until now.

00:26:02.578 --> 00:26:03.436
You're joking, right?

00:26:03.502 --> 00:26:04.647
Do I look like I'm joking?

00:26:06.431 --> 00:26:08.016
Why do you think I
drive everywhere, sam?

00:26:09.139 --> 00:26:10.923
All right. Uh, I'll go.

00:26:11.212 --> 00:26:11.608
What?

00:26:11.630 --> 00:26:12.665
I'll do this oneon my own.

00:26:13.216 --> 00:26:14.008
Are you, nuts?

00:26:14.559 --> 00:26:15.924
You said that the plane's gonna crash.

00:26:15.968 --> 00:26:17.972
Dean, we can do it together,
or I can do this for myself.

00:26:18.016 --> 00:26:19.887
I'm not seeing a third option, here.

00:26:20.658 --> 00:26:21.583
Come on!

00:26:23.279 --> 00:26:23.962
Really?

00:26:26.274 --> 00:26:27.132
Man...

00:26:40.056 --> 00:26:42.015
Just try to relax. Just try to shut up.

00:27:11.878 --> 00:27:12.847
You're humming Metallica?

00:27:12.869 --> 00:27:14.014
Calms me down.

00:27:16.172 --> 00:27:17.031
Look, man,

00:27:17.405 --> 00:27:18.528
I get you're nervous, all right?

00:27:18.550 --> 00:27:20.113
But you got to stay focused.

00:27:21.452 --> 00:27:21.959
Okay.

00:27:21.981 --> 00:27:22.883
I mean, we got

00:27:22.994 --> 00:27:25.834
32 minutes and counting
to track this thing down

00:27:25.878 --> 00:27:29.159
Or who Everit's possessing, anyway
and perform a full-On exorcism.

00:27:29.181 --> 00:27:31.360
On a crowded plane.That's gonna be easy.

00:27:31.449 --> 00:27:33.078
Take it one step at a time, all right?

00:27:34.792 --> 00:27:35.540
Now,

00:27:35.662 --> 00:27:37.687
Who is it possessing?

00:27:38.766 --> 00:27:40.020
It's usually gonna be somebody

00:27:40.021 --> 00:27:41.078
With some sort of weakness, you know,

00:27:41.100 --> 00:27:43.214
A chink in the armor that
the demon can worm through,

00:27:43.621 --> 00:27:46.395
Somebody with an addiction
or emotional distress.

00:27:48.476 --> 00:27:49.071
Well,

00:27:49.269 --> 00:27:51.030
This is Amanda's first
flight after the crash.

00:27:51.074 --> 00:27:52.682
If I were her, I'd be pretty messed up.

00:27:52.748 --> 00:27:53.452
Mm-Hmm.

00:27:55.324 --> 00:27:56.204
Excuse me.

00:27:56.730 --> 00:27:57.479
Are you Amanda?

00:27:57.633 --> 00:27:58.470
No, I'm not.

00:27:58.514 --> 00:28:00.341
Oh, my mistake.

00:28:06.265 --> 00:28:08.313
All right, well, that's got
to be amanda back there,so

00:28:09.106 --> 00:28:10.162
I'll go talk to her,

00:28:10.295 --> 00:28:12.342
And, uh, I'll get a
read on her mental state.

00:28:12.783 --> 00:28:14.082
What if she's already possessed?

00:28:15.427 --> 00:28:16.880
There's ways to test that.

00:28:19.082 --> 00:28:20.337
I brought holy water.

00:28:21.218 --> 00:28:22.957
No. I think we can go more subtle.

00:28:23.424 --> 00:28:25.604
If she's possessed, she'll
flinch at the name of god.

00:28:26.176 --> 00:28:27.123
Oh. Nice.

00:28:29.259 --> 00:28:29.941
Hey.

00:28:30.107 --> 00:28:30.789
What?

00:28:30.965 --> 00:28:31.846
Say it in latin.

00:28:32.132 --> 00:28:32.793
I know.

00:28:32.881 --> 00:28:33.453
Okay.

00:28:33.696 --> 00:28:34.334
Hey!

00:28:34.841 --> 00:28:35.655
What?!

00:28:35.964 --> 00:28:37.791
Uh, in latin, it's "Cristo."

00:28:37.901 --> 00:28:39.707
Dude, I know! I'm not an idiot!

00:28:52.582 --> 00:28:53.705
Hi. Hi.

00:28:54.762 --> 00:28:55.841
Can I help you with something?

00:28:55.929 --> 00:28:56.832
Oh, no.

00:28:56.876 --> 00:28:58.835
I'm just a bit of an uneasy flier.

00:28:59.200 --> 00:29:00.851
It makes me feel better to
walk around a little bit.

00:29:00.961 --> 00:29:02.899
Oh, it happens to the best of us.

00:29:03.647 --> 00:29:06.686
Of course, you being a stewardess,
I guess flying comes easy to you.

00:29:07.820 --> 00:29:09.009
You'd be surprised.

00:29:09.339 --> 00:29:11.276
Really? You're a nervous flier?

00:29:11.959 --> 00:29:13.610
Yeah, maybe a little bit.

00:29:14.953 --> 00:29:16.605
How is it that,being a stewardess,

00:29:16.946 --> 00:29:18.025
You're scared to fly?

00:29:19.147 --> 00:29:20.381
Kind of a long story.

00:29:21.514 --> 00:29:23.100
Right. I'm sorry for asking.

00:29:23.177 --> 00:29:23.981
It's okay.

00:29:25.335 --> 00:29:26.942
You ever consider other employment?

00:29:28.219 --> 00:29:29.034
No.

00:29:29.562 --> 00:29:31.214
Look, everybody's scared of something.

00:29:31.269 --> 00:29:32.656
I just, uh...

00:29:33.449 --> 00:29:35.408
I'm not gonna let it hold me back.

00:29:36.685 --> 00:29:37.412
Huh.

00:29:38.436 --> 00:29:39.074
So...

00:29:41.893 --> 00:29:42.685
Cristo.

00:29:43.984 --> 00:29:45.305
I'm sorry. Did you say something?

00:29:50.547 --> 00:29:51.405
Cristo?

00:29:52.572 --> 00:29:53.783
I-I didn't, I didn't

00:29:54.818 --> 00:29:56.095
Yeah, nothing. Never mind.

00:30:00.296 --> 00:30:01.155
Okay.

00:30:09.100 --> 00:30:11.962
All right, well, she's got to be the
most well-Adjusted person on the planet.

00:30:12.006 --> 00:30:13.063
You said "cristo"? Yeah.

00:30:13.107 --> 00:30:14.439
And? There's no demon in her.

00:30:14.461 --> 00:30:16.024
There's no demon getting in her.

00:30:16.090 --> 00:30:17.874
So, if it's on the
plane, it can be anyone...

00:30:18.006 --> 00:30:19.063
Anywhere.

00:30:19.856 --> 00:30:22.035
Come on! That can't be normal! Hey, hey,

00:30:22.113 --> 00:30:24.447
It's just a little turbulence.

00:30:24.777 --> 00:30:26.340
Sam, this plane is going to crash, okay?

00:30:26.385 --> 00:30:27.838
So quit treating me
like I'm friggin' fool.

00:30:27.926 --> 00:30:29.709
You need to calm down.
No, I'm sorry I can't.

00:30:29.753 --> 00:30:31.063
Yes, you can.

00:30:31.459 --> 00:30:34.388
Dude, Stow the touchy-Feely,
self-Help yoga crap.

00:30:34.432 --> 00:30:35.489
It's not helping. Listen,
if you're panicked,

00:30:35.533 --> 00:30:36.744
You're wide opento demonic possession,

00:30:36.766 --> 00:30:38.836
So you need to calm yourself down

00:30:38.946 --> 00:30:39.936
Right now.

00:30:48.901 --> 00:30:49.694
Good.

00:30:50.971 --> 00:30:51.719
Now,

00:30:52.325 --> 00:30:54.659
I found an exorcism in here
that I think is gonna work

00:30:55.254 --> 00:30:56.487
The ritual romano.

00:30:57.544 --> 00:30:58.424
What do we have to do?

00:30:58.887 --> 00:30:59.680
It's two parts.

00:30:59.724 --> 00:31:02.146
The first part expels the
demon from the victim's body.

00:31:02.301 --> 00:31:05.405
It makes it manifest, which
actually makes it more powerful.

00:31:05.680 --> 00:31:06.451
More powerful?

00:31:06.561 --> 00:31:07.463
Yeah. How?

00:31:08.146 --> 00:31:09.599
Well, it doesn't need to
possess someone anymore.

00:31:09.643 --> 00:31:11.471
It can just wreak havoc on its own.

00:31:11.735 --> 00:31:13.298
Oh. And why is that a good thing?

00:31:13.827 --> 00:31:15.808
Well, because the second part

00:31:16.689 --> 00:31:18.164
Sends the bastard back to hell

00:31:18.561 --> 00:31:19.728
Once and for all.

00:31:21.247 --> 00:31:22.942
First thing's first we got to find it.

00:32:00.491 --> 00:32:01.423
Ohh! Don't do that.

00:32:01.531 --> 00:32:02.333
Anything?

00:32:02.527 --> 00:32:04.390
No, nothing. How much time we got?

00:32:04.650 --> 00:32:05.538
15 minutes.

00:32:06.795 --> 00:32:08.116
Maybe we missed somebody.

00:32:08.874 --> 00:32:10.390
Maybe the thing's just not on the plane.

00:32:11.660 --> 00:32:12.613
You believe that?

00:32:13.371 --> 00:32:14.454
Well, I will if you will.

00:32:23.958 --> 00:32:24.933
What? What is it?

00:32:26.255 --> 00:32:26.969
Cristo.

00:32:42.116 --> 00:32:43.286
She's not gonna believe this.

00:32:43.437 --> 00:32:44.476
12 minutes, dude.

00:32:46.890 --> 00:32:47.735
Oh, hi.

00:32:48.491 --> 00:32:50.084
Flight's not too bumpy for you, I hope.

00:32:50.157 --> 00:32:52.330
Actually, that's kind of what
we need to talk to you about.

00:32:52.547 --> 00:32:54.430
Um, okay.What can I do for you?

00:32:54.913 --> 00:32:56.507
This is gonna sound nuts, but

00:32:56.871 --> 00:32:59.165
We just don't have time for the whole
"the true this out there" speech right now.

00:32:59.213 --> 00:33:01.362
Look, we know you were on flight 2485.

00:33:03.098 --> 00:33:04.040
Who are you guys?

00:33:04.160 --> 00:33:06.309
Now, we've spoken to
some other survivors.

00:33:06.430 --> 00:33:08.820
We know something brought down that
plane and it wasn't a mechanical failure.

00:33:08.893 --> 00:33:09.907
We need your help

00:33:09.979 --> 00:33:11.694
Because we need to stop
from happening again.

00:33:11.814 --> 00:33:12.716
Here. Now. I'm sorry

00:33:12.788 --> 00:33:15.638
Here. I-I'm very busy. Whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa. Wait a second.

00:33:15.710 --> 00:33:17.110
I'm not gonna hurt you, okay?

00:33:17.255 --> 00:33:18.631
But listen to me, huh...

00:33:18.752 --> 00:33:21.039
The pilot in 2485, Chuck Lambert.

00:33:21.160 --> 00:33:22.029
He's dead.

00:33:22.712 --> 00:33:23.750
Wait. What?

00:33:23.919 --> 00:33:25.126
What, Chuck is dead?

00:33:25.416 --> 00:33:26.961
He died in a plane crash.

00:33:27.106 --> 00:33:28.652
That's two plane crashes in two months.

00:33:28.676 --> 00:33:30.318
That doesn't strike you as strange?

00:33:31.066 --> 00:33:32.853
Look, there was
something wrong with 2485.

00:33:32.878 --> 00:33:34.203
Now maybe you're
sensitive maybe you didn't

00:33:34.228 --> 00:33:35.628
But there's something
wrong with this flight, too.

00:33:35.653 --> 00:33:37.303
Amanda,you have to believe us.

00:33:42.609 --> 00:33:43.534
On...

00:33:44.484 --> 00:33:46.209
On 2485,

00:33:46.259 --> 00:33:48.059
There was this man.

00:33:48.109 --> 00:33:50.234
He...had these eyes.

00:33:50.509 --> 00:33:52.162
Yes. That's exactly
what we're talking about.

00:33:52.184 --> 00:33:53.837
I don't understand what
are you asking me to do?

00:33:53.859 --> 00:33:55.648
Okay. The copilot, we need
you bring him back here.

00:33:55.693 --> 00:33:57.754
Why? What does he have
to do with anything?

00:33:57.821 --> 00:33:58.750
Don't have time to explain.

00:33:58.772 --> 00:34:00.199
We just need to talk to him. Okay?

00:34:00.312 --> 00:34:01.693
How am I supposed to go in the cockpit

00:34:01.738 --> 00:34:03.572
And get the copilot--
Do whatever it takes

00:34:03.617 --> 00:34:05.293
Tell him there's
something broken back here,

00:34:05.338 --> 00:34:06.719
Whatever will get him
out of that cockpit.

00:34:06.787 --> 00:34:08.213
Do you know that I could lose my job

00:34:08.236 --> 00:34:10.410
If you -- You're gonna lose a
lot more if you don't help us out.

00:34:17.008 --> 00:34:17.755
Okay.

00:34:57.834 --> 00:34:58.989
Yeah, what's the problem?

00:35:05.170 --> 00:35:07.841
Wait. What are you doing? You said
you were just gonna talk to him.

00:35:07.887 --> 00:35:09.358
We are gonna talk to him.

00:35:18.397 --> 00:35:19.718
Oh, my god.What's wrong with him?

00:35:19.784 --> 00:35:20.709
Look. We need you calm.

00:35:20.753 --> 00:35:22.537
We need you outside the curtain.
Well, I don't underst..., I don't know

00:35:22.581 --> 00:35:24.166
Don't let anybody in,
okay? Can you do that?

00:35:24.210 --> 00:35:25.487
Can you do that?

00:35:25.795 --> 00:35:26.380
Amanda?

00:35:26.623 --> 00:35:27.177
Okay.

00:35:27.907 --> 00:35:28.483
Okay.

00:35:30.161 --> 00:35:32.331
Hurry up, sam. I don't know
how much longer I can hold him.

00:35:54.248 --> 00:35:55.842
I know what happened to your girlfriend!

00:35:57.768 --> 00:35:59.318
She must have died screaming!

00:36:00.004 --> 00:36:01.642
Even now, she's burning!

00:36:04.551 --> 00:36:05.260
Sam!

00:36:08.865 --> 00:36:10.038
"Prayer"...

00:36:12.761 --> 00:36:13.470
I got him.

00:36:34.398 --> 00:36:35.018
Where'd he go?

00:36:35.085 --> 00:36:35.992
He's in the plane.

00:36:36.059 --> 00:36:37.564
Hurry up.We got to finish it.

00:38:24.895 --> 00:38:25.426
I don't know.

00:38:25.515 --> 00:38:26.733
I was walking through the airport,

00:38:26.976 --> 00:38:28.283
Then it all goes blank.

00:38:28.570 --> 00:38:30.740
I don't even remember
getting on the plane.

00:38:32.751 --> 00:38:33.902
Anything else?

00:38:34.279 --> 00:38:35.186
No, that's all.

00:38:38.968 --> 00:38:39.920
"Thank you"

00:38:46.318 --> 00:38:47.337
Let's get out of here.

00:38:50.281 --> 00:38:51.123
You okay?

00:38:52.827 --> 00:38:53.580
Dean,

00:38:55.550 --> 00:38:57.166
It knew about Jessica.

00:38:59.841 --> 00:39:02.210
Sam, these things,t-They read minds.

00:39:02.586 --> 00:39:03.317
They lie.

00:39:04.091 --> 00:39:05.309
All right?That's all it was.

00:39:06.992 --> 00:39:07.612
Yeah.

00:39:10.054 --> 00:39:10.829
Come on.

00:39:17.028 --> 00:39:19.370
Nobody knows what you
guys did, but i do.

00:39:20.787 --> 00:39:22.470
A lot of people could have been killed.

00:39:23.931 --> 00:39:25.277
Your dad's gonna be real proud.

00:39:25.808 --> 00:39:27.137
We'll see you around, Jerry.

00:39:30.369 --> 00:39:31.344
You know, Jerry.

00:39:31.676 --> 00:39:32.251
Yeah.

00:39:32.867 --> 00:39:35.480
I meant to ask you how did you
get my cellphone number, anyway?

00:39:35.524 --> 00:39:37.162
I've only had it for like six months.

00:39:37.428 --> 00:39:38.624
Your dad gave it to me.

00:39:39.266 --> 00:39:39.704
What?

00:39:39.749 --> 00:39:41.077
When did you talk to him?

00:39:41.254 --> 00:39:43.690
I mean, I didn't exactly talk to him,but

00:39:44.110 --> 00:39:46.767
I called his number. His voice
message said to give you a call.

00:39:48.711 --> 00:39:49.508
Thanks again, guys.

00:40:06.400 --> 00:40:07.884
This doesn't make any sense, man.

00:40:07.906 --> 00:40:10.054
I've called dad's number like 50 times.

00:40:10.077 --> 00:40:11.383
It's been out of service.

00:40:12.706 --> 00:40:13.902
This is John Winchester.

00:40:14.234 --> 00:40:15.540
I can't be reached.

00:40:15.549 --> 00:40:17.896
If this is an emergency,
call my son, Dean

00:40:18.848 --> 00:40:23.648

866-907-3235

00:40:24.644 --> 00:40:25.729
He'll can help.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
